00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:34.530
So how many of you
know what Sling TV is?

00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:36.860
Oh, that's so many.

00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:38.900
For those of you who
don't know, Sling TV

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:41.780
is an online TV
platform where users

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:48.040
can sign on and watch online
live TV and on-demand content.

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:50.270
And like so many other
subscription services,

00:05:50.270 --> 00:05:52.910
we're concerned
with customer churn.

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:55.860
We want to identify the
customers before they churn,

00:05:55.860 --> 00:05:59.000
so we can do something about it.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:03.030
For this binary
classification problem,

00:06:03.030 --> 00:06:06.480
we can look at so many
different features.

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:09.770
For example, what
users watched, what

00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:12.050
channel they watch,
how long they

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:15.510
watch it for, what day of
the week, and the time slot.

00:06:15.510 --> 00:06:16.740
This is just an example.

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:20.790
You can look at
millions of attributes.

00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:23.120
So for this churn
prediction problem,

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:25.490
let's assume that we look
at six days of activity

00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:28.940
and want to predict
churn at day 30.

00:06:28.940 --> 00:06:33.290
For this one user, the user
subscribes on the first day

00:06:33.290 --> 00:06:39.080
and watches ESPN
for 1,500 seconds.

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:41.300
And it's a Monday night.

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.070
They come back again
on the second day.

00:06:43.070 --> 00:06:48.770
They watch Food Network and
it's Tuesday 6:00 to 8:00 PM.

00:06:48.770 --> 00:06:50.810
They don't watch
anything on day 3 and 4,

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:53.630
and they come back again and
watch some Travel Channel

00:06:53.630 --> 00:06:56.480
on a Friday morning.

00:06:56.480 --> 00:06:59.330
For many non-deep
learning models,

00:06:59.330 --> 00:07:01.770
this data needs to be
aggregated per user.

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:04.580
So for that one user, you
will have total number

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:07.850
of seconds watched,
channel most watched,

00:07:07.850 --> 00:07:10.520
total number of sessions.

00:07:10.520 --> 00:07:14.003
Was it mostly a weekday or
weekend, and most common time

00:07:14.003 --> 00:07:15.650
slot.

00:07:15.650 --> 00:07:18.740
However, this kind of model
will disregard the daily pattern

00:07:18.740 --> 00:07:19.820
of user activity.

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:25.370
There are these studies
online, the papers that

00:07:25.370 --> 00:07:30.020
use convolutional neural
networks for churn prediction,

00:07:30.020 --> 00:07:34.400
and they use daily patterns,
daily activities of users.

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:38.150
The model architecture
for this kind of model

00:07:38.150 --> 00:07:41.150
is that it has multiple
convolutional layers, followed

00:07:41.150 --> 00:07:46.020
by max pooling, and then it
gets to a fully connected layer.

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:49.730
And then it will get to a final
softmax or a sigmoid output

00:07:49.730 --> 00:07:51.794
for the final classification.

