00:08:03.630 --> 00:08:06.840
SALMA RIAZI: In order to
use this kind of model,

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:10.980
we need to clarify between days
of activity and inactivity.

00:08:10.980 --> 00:08:13.680
So for the days that the
user has been inactive,

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:16.170
we need to insert zeros.

00:08:16.170 --> 00:08:19.050
For example for the
days 3, 4, and 6,

00:08:19.050 --> 00:08:21.600
we insert zeros for
the numerical values

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:25.570
and encode the categoricals.

00:08:25.570 --> 00:08:30.220
Then before feeding this
data into the model,

00:08:30.220 --> 00:08:33.549
the data needs to be
encoded and scaled.

00:08:33.549 --> 00:08:36.830
For numericals it needs to
be scaled between 0 and 1.

00:08:36.830 --> 00:08:41.250
And for categoricals
it needs to be encoded.

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:45.450
So after trying that, we were
able to improve our model

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:49.830
metric by 15% compared to
our baseline on deep learning

00:08:49.830 --> 00:08:51.090
models.

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:54.270
For that one sample,
if you look at one user

00:08:54.270 --> 00:08:58.470
for six days of activity,
with five features

00:08:58.470 --> 00:09:03.220
it's very simple to preprocess
and train the model.

00:09:03.220 --> 00:09:07.530
However, with many, if you want
to look at a more granular time

00:09:07.530 --> 00:09:10.420
standard, for example
minutes or hours;

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:13.630
and for millions of users
with thousands of features,

00:09:13.630 --> 00:09:16.020
this problem gets very
challenging really quick.

00:09:22.090 --> 00:09:24.160
So now I'm going
to talk about how

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:27.550
I did the preprocessing
and each iteration.

00:09:30.330 --> 00:09:35.160
First I started small
with a data warehouse.

00:09:35.160 --> 00:09:37.930
I moved the data to
a virtual machine,

00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:40.760
preprocessed and saved the
data on the virtual machine

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:42.270
using Pandas and NumPy.

00:09:42.270 --> 00:09:44.970
I'm going to get into the
details in the future slides.

00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:48.560
I trained the model.

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:50.540
It was a Keras model
on the virtual machine,

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:53.210
the predictions on
the virtual machine.

00:09:53.210 --> 00:09:55.820
The only thing is that
I needed to preprocess

00:09:55.820 --> 00:09:59.030
the predictions the same way
