00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:07.130
And then I saved the predictions
to the original database.

00:10:07.130 --> 00:10:11.580
So we realized quickly
that that system,

00:10:11.580 --> 00:10:13.200
it was not good for production.

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:14.570
It's not very scalable.

00:10:14.570 --> 00:10:19.380
And we wanted to move towards
a serverless scalable system.

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:24.740
So we started changing our
tools and moving through GCP.

00:10:24.740 --> 00:10:29.870
First, I started with
an original database,

00:10:29.870 --> 00:10:32.300
moved it to Google Storage
and did the preprocessing

00:10:32.300 --> 00:10:37.070
on Datalab, using the same
functions and same tools.

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:40.520
I saved the preprocessed
data to Google Storage,

00:10:40.520 --> 00:10:45.680
did the training with Keras
on CMLE Cloud Machine Learning

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:50.000
Services, and did the
predictions on virtual machine.

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:52.070
I did this because
last year Keras was not

00:10:52.070 --> 00:10:53.720
compatible with the model API.

00:10:53.720 --> 00:10:56.810
But I think today,
things are different.

00:10:56.810 --> 00:10:58.610
After that, I did
the predictions

00:10:58.610 --> 00:11:01.910
