00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:08.530
Again, I needed to do the
preprocessing on the prediction

00:11:08.530 --> 00:11:09.030
data.

00:11:12.530 --> 00:11:15.380
This is detail about the
code I used for the first two

00:11:15.380 --> 00:11:17.570
iterations.

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:23.720
First I read the unloaded CSV
file into a Pandas data frame.

00:11:23.720 --> 00:11:28.070
Then I scaled and
encoded the data,

00:11:28.070 --> 00:11:30.140
and then I set it
an NumPy array,

00:11:30.140 --> 00:11:37.200
while inserting zeros for
the reason I showed earlier.

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:39.820
And then I saved the
NumPy and pickle files.

00:11:39.820 --> 00:11:42.480
The encoding, I did
the encoding using

00:11:42.480 --> 00:11:46.140
LabelEncoder and
StandardScaler by Scikit-learn.

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:48.030
I saved the two
